values.content:
=You are a senior content writer. Write a blog post draft.

Topic: {{ $json.Topic }}
Audience: {{ $json.Audience }}
Key points to cover:
{{ $json['Key points (one per line)'] }}

Format your reply EXACTLY like this:
TITLE: <one compelling title, max 60 characters>
BODY:
<the post in clean HTML: a short intro paragraph, one <h2> section per key point with 2-3 paragraphs each, and a closing section with a call to action. No <html> or <body> tags. 800-1200 words. Write plainly - no buzzwords, no fluff.>

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $input.first().json.message.content;
const titleMatch = raw.match(/TITLE:\s*(.+)/);
const bodyMatch = raw.match(/BODY:\s*([\s\S]+)/);
return [{ json: {
  title: titleMatch ? titleMatch[1].trim() : 'Untitled draft',
  content: bodyMatch ? bodyMatch[1].trim() : raw
} }];
